# Template for github.key: the token that lets THIS machine write to the
# Manikin-Catalog repo (SWFs in swfs/<path>, the catalog in catalog.json.gz).
#
# Never commit the real file, and never build it into a published exe - anyone
# could extract it and push to the repo every copy downloads from. Without a
# token the app is read-only and saves fall back to Supabase.
#
# Fine-grained token, scoped to Manikin-Catalog only, with:
#   Repository permissions -> Contents: Read and write
# Expiration: "No expiration" is allowed for fine-grained tokens, unless the
# org (or enterprise) sets a maximum lifetime - the org default caps it at 366
# days. The scheduled snapshot does not use this token at all.
# MANIKIN_GITHUB_TOKEN overrides this file.
token=github_pat_your_token_here
